//! `ui` — Bezel kit widgets on top of Zeus, in the declarative syntax.
//!
//! The barrel re-exports every kit widget as a thin wrapper (each calls the
//! implementing file qualified, so nothing recurses). Apps import this file
//! and call `Button`, `Chip`, `Tabs`, … unqualified — no `ui.` / `zeus.`
//! prefix. Because the wrappers are declarations of this module, they shadow
//! the same-named std:zeus widgets for any app that imports this barrel —
//! that is the layering: kit widgets replace the raw std ones.
//!
//! Example:
//! ```
//! import "std:zeus"
//! import "../packages/zeus-components/ui.yuga"
//!
//! fn main() {
//!     App("Hello", 400, 300, fn() {
//!         Box(align_direction = DIRECTION.Column, background = canvas(), padding = SPACE.Page, spacing = SPACE.Section) {
//!             Card() {
//!                 CardHeader(title = "Hello", subtitle = "A short subtitle"),
//!                 Chip(label = "live", color = accent()),
//!             }
//!         }
//!     })
//! }
//! ```
//!
//! Widgets take props as named arguments (`size = sm()`, `look = solid()`);
//! containers take children in a trailing block. Handlers ride in as
//! `on_press` / `on_click` props. Each widget file holds its own `*Props`
//! struct and defines its public name directly.

